{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","title":"thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.md","line":385,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex#thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","label":"thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","line":724,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Tangential Gauss equation]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0111}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form, rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.2.4}\n  For $X,Y,Z,W$ tangent to a hypersurface $H$ with induced metric $g_H$ and\n  induced curvature $R^H$,\n  \\[\n    g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H\\big(R^H(X,Y)Z,W\\big)-\\Pi(X,W)\\Pi(Y,Z)+\\Pi(X,Z)\\Pi(Y,W).\n  \\]\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation}\n  \\sketch\n  Using \\cref{def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form}, the induced connection is\n  $\\nabla^H_XY=(\\nabla_XY)^\\top=\\nabla_XY+\\Pi(X,Y)N$. Substitute\n  $\\nabla_XY=\\nabla^H_XY-\\Pi(X,Y)N$ into $R(X,Y)Z$ and separate tangent and normal\n  parts. Pairing the tangent part with $W$ gives\n  \\[\n   g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H(R^H(X,Y)Z,W)\n   -\\Pi(X,W)\\Pi(Y,Z)+\\Pi(X,Z)\\Pi(Y,W).\n  \\]\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Tangential Gauss equation] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368332d74616e67656e7469616c2d6375727661747572652d6571756174696f6e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0111</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-second-fundamental-form\">↗ def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23rem%3Apet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition\">↗ rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:3.2.4</span></span>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X,Y,Z,W$\">$X,Y,Z,W$</span> tangent to a hypersurface <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H$\">$H$</span> with induced metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_H$\">$g_H$</span> and induced curvature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$R^H$\">$R^H$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H\\big(R^H(X,Y)Z,W\\big)-\\Pi (X,W)\\Pi (Y,Z)+\\Pi (X,Z)\\Pi (Y,W).  \\]\">\\[  g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H\\big(R^H(X,Y)Z,W\\big)-\\Pi (X,W)\\Pi (Y,Z)+\\Pi (X,Z)\\Pi (Y,W).  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23thm%3Apet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation\">↗ thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation</a> \\sketch Using <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_Curvature%23def%3Apet-ch3-second-fundamental-form\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368332d7365636f6e642d66756e64616d656e74616c2d666f726d\">subsection 2.1</a>, the induced connection is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla ^H_XY=(\\nabla _XY)^\\top =\\nabla _XY+\\Pi (X,Y)N$\">$\\nabla ^H_XY=(\\nabla _XY)^\\top =\\nabla _XY+\\Pi (X,Y)N$</span>. Substitute <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla _XY=\\nabla ^H_XY-\\Pi (X,Y)N$\">$\\nabla _XY=\\nabla ^H_XY-\\Pi (X,Y)N$</span> into <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$R(X,Y)Z$\">$R(X,Y)Z$</span> and separate tangent and normal parts. Pairing the tangent part with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span> gives </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H(R^H(X,Y)Z,W) -\\Pi (X,W)\\Pi (Y,Z)+\\Pi (X,Z)\\Pi (Y,W).  \\]\">\\[  g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H(R^H(X,Y)Z,W) -\\Pi (X,W)\\Pi (Y,Z)+\\Pi (X,Z)\\Pi (Y,W).  \\]</span></p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-normal-curvature-equation","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form","title":"def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form","label":"def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition","title":"rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition","label":"rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","title":"thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","label":"thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","title":"thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","label":"thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-normal-curvature-equation","title":"thm:pet-ch3-normal-curvature-equation","label":"thm:pet-ch3-normal-curvature-equation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-curvature-equations-by-dimension","title":"rem:pet-ch3-curvature-equations-by-dimension","label":"rem:pet-ch3-curvature-equations-by-dimension"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#cor:pet-ch3-gauss-egregium","title":"cor:pet-ch3-gauss-egregium","label":"cor:pet-ch3-gauss-egregium"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ex-4","title":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-4","label":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ex-11","title":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-11","label":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-11"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-ex-21","title":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-21","label":"rem:pet-ch3-ex-21"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","title":"thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[Tangential Gauss equation]\n  \\label{thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0111}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form, rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.2.4}\n  For $X,Y,Z,W$ tangent to a hypersurface $H$ with induced metric $g_H$ and\n  induced curvature $R^H$,\n  \\[\n    g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H\\big(R^H(X,Y)Z,W\\big)-\\Pi(X,W)\\Pi(Y,Z)+\\Pi(X,Z)\\Pi(Y,W).\n  \\]\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch3-tangential-curvature-equation}\n  \\sketch\n  Using \\cref{def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form}, the induced connection is\n  $\\nabla^H_XY=(\\nabla_XY)^\\top=\\nabla_XY+\\Pi(X,Y)N$. Substitute\n  $\\nabla_XY=\\nabla^H_XY-\\Pi(X,Y)N$ into $R(X,Y)Z$ and separate tangent and normal\n  parts. Pairing the tangent part with $W$ gives\n  \\[\n   g(R(X,Y)Z,W)=g_H(R^H(X,Y)Z,W)\n   -\\Pi(X,W)\\Pi(Y,Z)+\\Pi(X,Z)\\Pi(Y,W).\n  \\]\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form","title":"def:pet-ch3-second-fundamental-form","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_Curvature#rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition","title":"rem:pet-ch3-tangential-normal-decomposition","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}